n makes this clean.\n\n### D2: Tag Index Structure\n\nTwo indexes maintained in parallel:\n- `_key_tags: dict[key, frozenset]` — maps each cached key to its set of tags\n- `_tag_keys: dict[str, set]` — maps each tag to the set of keys carrying it\n\n**Rationale**: O(1) lookup for tag->keys, O(1) for key->tags. Both updated on put/delete/eviction.\n\n### D3: Validation Before Mutation\n\nAll validation (maxsize type, tags type/contents) is performed before any call to the underlying LRUCache or any index mutation.\n\n**Rationale**: Requirement R01 explicitly states ValueError must be raised \"before changing existing state.\"\n\n### D4: Eviction Handling\n\nLRUCache's `popitem()` is overridden via the composition pattern. When the underlying cache evicts an entry, TaggedCache intercepts the eviction to clean up tag indexes.\n\n**Rationale**: R02 requires \"LRU eviction must not leave stale memberships.\"\n\n### D5: No `maxsize` Setter\n\n`maxsize` is set once at construction. There is no public setter. If a user needs a different maxsize, they create a new TaggedCache.\n\n**Rationale**: The spec says \"Invalid replacement input must leave the old value unchanged\" — since there is no setter, this is trivially satisfied. If a setter is needed later, it can be added with full validation.\nPLAN_EOF", "exit_code": 0, "stderr": "", "stdout": ""}